# six closures over one scope and two numbers. A slot that leaves its closure unmade is four bytes wide, and so is the word of the scope: the slots are laid behind the choice of their forms, each by its width:
# 6 x 4 for the closures, 4 for the scope, 2 x 8 for the numbers, behind 16 bytes of header: 60 bytes, a cell of 64. With each slot alone in eight bytes it was 16 + 8 x 8 = 80.
# with typed slots withheld the numbers are boxed, eight bytes as well, and the cell has the word of the extra properties at 16: the closures follow beside it from 20 on, four bytes each, and the scope behind them: a cell of 64, as with typed slots.
# with the deferral withheld no slot has that form.
# -- source: closures-that-a-literal-leaves-unmade-take-four-bytes-each.ts
# declare function sink(...values: unknown[]): void;
